WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.634
- Who took a bite of this?

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.967
- (laughs collectively)

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.960
- Hey, I'm Kelly and I'm a
Culinary Producer at Tasty.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.490
And this is my husband, Jeremy.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.090
- Hi, I'm Jeremy and I'm a chef.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.720
- And we have been cooking
together for 11 years?

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.650
- Yeah, that sounds about right.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.250
- We met in culinary school.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.810
Day one, he fell in love. I didn't.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:35.643
- Wow.

00:00:35.643 --> 00:00:36.476
- I'm joking.

00:00:36.476 --> 00:00:39.430
- We have two wonderful
young boys, Dylan and Teddy,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.340
and Dylan will be joining us today.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.440
- [Producer] Are you nervous at all?

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.030
- No, I feel great.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.400
- [Dylan] I'm nervous...

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.460
- Why? Cause you have to pick
between mommy and daddy, yeah.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.430
- [Producer] Is there
any like challenge stakes

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.370
we could add to this?

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:54.390
- If I win, I would love
some help with the laundry

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.980
this whole seven loads a week thing

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.110
isn't working for me anymore.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.080
Maybe split it up.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.360
- Fine, okay. So what happens if I win?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.210
- I'll wake up before 9:00 AM.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.680
- Yeah, I wanna sleep in on the weekends.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.513
- You got it.

00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:06.346
- Okay. Deal.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.470
For today's challenge,

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.610
I'm gonna be making a space
themed pizza lunch box.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.950
We are going to start with easy,
peasy pizza dough in a can.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.150
So I have this cute rocket
shaped cookie cutter.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.520
I'm gonna cut out a few, kind of small.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.980
I don't know how many stuff it with pizza.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.030
All right, let's do one,

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.440
and then assess, if I have
to change my game plan.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.490
So this is just store bought pizza sauce.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.600
Again, store bought is fine.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.433
They don't care.

00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:34.670
So I'm just gonna put like
the teeniest little amount

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.853
and then I'm gonna add some cheese.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.493
And then I found these
little baby pepperonis

00:01:40.493 --> 00:01:41.830
that I thought were so cute.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.220
Now I'm just gonna wash the
outer part, the outer like rim,

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.120
so I can stick another piece
on top and glue it together.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.020
Kind of just looks like a Christmas tree.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.380
It definitely lost its shape.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.280
That's okay. That's okay.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.660
Alright. I also have this rocket.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.060
Maybe this will look better.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.130
Okay. This one's cute.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.370
All right, so I'm just gonna brush the top

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.830
with egg wash to get it nice and crispy.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:06.000
And then I was just gonna
put a little Parmesan on top.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.570
So it's like half pizza,
half cheesy breadstick.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.803
And then maybe I should
make a little window.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.900
Okay. So I'm gonna bake these at 425°,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.490
I think for like eight to
10 minutes, but we'll see.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.530
I wanted to recreate those
like little pudding packs

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.210
but I wanted to make a healthier version.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:26.850
It's called ABC pudding,
avocado, banana, and cacao.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.370
And then I'm gonna call it galaxy pudding

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.390
and dye some whipped
cream, blue and purple,

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.950
and swirl it on top.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.900
So it's like outer space theme,
but a little bit healthier.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.440
First thing, A is avocado.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.160
I could not find any good
avocados at the store.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.750
So I actually found these frozen ones.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.360
So they look pretty green.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.760
So we're gonna add those in
and it'll probably give it

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.900
like a nice texture that it's frozen.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:50.923
Add one banana.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.220
And then the C is cocoa powder

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.420
which is where the chocolate comes in.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.330
Dylan has the biggest sweet tooth.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.120
He asks for cookies
and cake every morning.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.000
I have to tell him it's
not a breakfast food.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.870
So I think he'll be
really excited about this.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:06.930
And then just to sweeten it up

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.630
I'm gonna add some maple syrup.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.680
I'm gonna add a little bit of milk

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.410
just to like help it blend together.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.830
And then how easy was that?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:14.663
We're just gonna blend it up.

00:03:14.663 --> 00:03:17.306
(blender whirring)

00:03:17.306 --> 00:03:21.760
(amplified blender whirring)

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.593
That's perfect.

00:03:22.593 --> 00:03:23.490
He is gonna love this.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.980
This might be my winning star.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.110
The next step I'm gonna do for my lunchbox

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.880
is add some fruit and veggies.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.560
Just to add some balance to
the pizza and the pudding.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.930
So I'm just gonna cut some thick slices

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.133
and then take my star cookie cutter.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.120
Look how cute!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.360
Then for the bell pepper
I was actually thinking

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.880
it could be like the
fire, the gas, what is it?

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.780
So I'm just gonna cut it in
thin strips then maybe in half

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.450
and then like, here's the rocket ship,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.550
and then I'll put 'em
underneath like that.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.790
Carrots too. Dylan loves
carrots and hummus.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.080
So we got our veggies.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.773
Now let's move on to the fruit.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.350
Look how juicy that is.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.050
First, I'm just gonna cut some circles.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.420
I mean, I guess it's a full moon

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.520
but maybe I should make it a little cuter.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.230
Cute.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.290
Okay, I wanted to create
some type of Martian alien

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.670
to go with the space theme.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:20.503
So I found this little cheese

00:04:20.503 --> 00:04:23.123
and I'm gonna pull the wax off,

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.270
and then cut it down the middle.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.080
And then I'm gonna use
some marshmallow fluff

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.510
to glue on some eyes.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.863
Kind of like the Toy Story Martian.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.270
I've never done this, but we'll see.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.570
I just have to tell Dylan
he can't eat the wax.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.970
I don't know, do they look like aliens?

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.500
Like? Maybe?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.220
Maybe, if I can like put
some toothpicks in his head.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.040
So I need to make a planet and
green is his favorite color.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.930
So I'm gonna take a Tootsie Roll Lollipop

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.903
and put a ring around it, to make Saturn.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.410
That's cute...

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.243
...right?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.900
No? (laughs)

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.270
To make like the green antennas

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.030
I'm gonna take some green apple

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.763
and little strips and
then stick it in the top.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.040
It kinda looks like a rabbit.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.640
It looks like a three eyed rabbit.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.520
Let's just move on.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.353
What do I have next?

00:05:10.353 --> 00:05:11.960
I gotta make the ranch dip, the best part.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.600
Okay, so we're just
gonna put some sour cream

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.160
and I'm going old school
with the ranch packet

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.510
because you cannot beat this flavor.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.630
Even as a chef, I know I've
made ranch a million times.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.910
It never tastes like this ever, ever.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.180
When I worked in a restaurant
and when I was a waitress,

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.650
I was in charge of making the ranch.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.200
People were always asking for the recipe

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.710
and I'm like (laughs) it's
on the back of the package.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.140
Okay, I'll put this in the fridge

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.430
and then move on to the next step.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.730
All right, we're onto the last step.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.420
I'm gonna make the galaxy whipped cream

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.110
to go onto our healthy pudding.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:47.030
So I'm just gonna take some heavy cream.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.260
I'm gonna add just a little bit of

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.290
powdered sugar to sweeten it.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.450
And then I'm just gonna beat this

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.120
with a hand mixer on high speed

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.180
until medium to stiff peaks form.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.970
Those are stiff peaks.
Little bit of purple.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:01.440
Ooh, this is like a neon
purple. This is fun.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.080
Okay, so we got purple done.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.210
Now let's add blue.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.450
I was a little bit nervous

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.020
the food dye would mess

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.200
with the texture of the whipped cream,

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.480
but it's actually working out.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.410
Okay, all right, and now
we're gonna do the fun part.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:14.820
We're gonna go to the assembly.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:18.100
First, I'm going to add my rocket ship

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.270
and then I'm gonna add some bell peppers

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.470
and some carrots coming off the end,

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:24.943
so it looks like it's
that fire spurting out.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:30.820
I have my star cucumbers and
then I also have my mango moons

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.090
with some blueberries cause
I know Dylan Love those.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.750
So now I have my alien Martains

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.860
We're still not sure about
these, but they're cute.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:38.760
They're cute.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.293
Okay. The best part, our healthy pudding.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.330
Look at those fun colors.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.200
He's gonna love that. He's gonna love it.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.600
And then for the all star,

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.680
I found these outer space themed sprinkles

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.800
and finally our little Saturn lollipop.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.302
And that's it.

00:06:56.302 --> 00:06:59.552
(spacey, sci-fi music)

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:13.500
- So today I will be cooking
a superhero themed lunch.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.140
I will be making a
Captain America burrito,

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.160
Captain America rice crispy treats,

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.110
little Spider-man strawberries,

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.820
and the hammers of Thor

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:24.040
using cheese and pretzel sticks.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.650
At home, we call Dylan "Captain America"

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.440
because he protects his little brother

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.660
who we call 'Iron Man'.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.990
So I think this one will
go over well with him.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.890
So first for the Rice Krispy treats,

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:36.620
we're gonna melt some butter,
the more fat the better.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.010
So now that the butter's melted,

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.693
I'm just gonna add in the marshmallows.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.940
Now that our marshmallow and
butter are nice and smooth

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.813
and all mixed together, we
will add the Rice Krispies.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.170
I'm just gonna mix it all together

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.740
until all forms one ball

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.490
and then we'll get it cooling down.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.500
All right, now they're all mixed together,

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.660
and we'll start cooling them down,

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.040
so we could shape them into
balls and into shields.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.770
So normally if I was
gonna Rice Krispy treats,

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.730
I would flatten this out
and try to compress it.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.220
But since we're just
rolling it into balls,

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.900
I'll just pop it into the fridge like this

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:14.733
and let it cool down.

00:08:14.733 --> 00:08:17.340
Now that they're cooled down,
I could add some sprinkles.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.920
If you add them while they're still warm,

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.382
the color will be bleed into them.

00:08:20.382 --> 00:08:22.140
And you'll just kind of have a brown mess

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.510
and then shape them
into balls and shields.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:27.040
And now we're gonna mix the sprinkles

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.947
into the Rice Krispy treats.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.830
Now, once they're mixed in,

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.870
we are just gonna roll
it into a little ball

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.120
and then flatten it out
to look like a shield.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.350
We're just gonna use a whole cutter

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:39.650
and punch out the center

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.863
to represent the star on his shield.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.630
So next we are going to
make Spider-man faces out of

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.820
strawberries, chocolate
chips and marshmallow fluff.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.550
So this is really simple.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.870
All we're gonna do is
slice the strawberries.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.620
So now we have our face.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:59.390
Next, we will place two
chocolate chips as the eyes,

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.650
try to wedge them in there.

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:03.780
And then we're gonna shape
those eyes with the white

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.130
to kind of make it look
like Spider-man's eyes.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.860
Okay, now we have small strawberries

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.270
that vaguely look like Spider-man.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:18.860
Next we're gonna cut cubes
out of a block of cheese

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:22.700
for Thor's hammer and put
pretzel sticks into the box.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.830
So make it look like a big hammer.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.950
So next up, I'm going
to try to make the fist

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.000
of the Incredible Hulk.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.410
The Hulk wears purple pants.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.950
So I'm going to take vanilla
yogurt and purple food coloring

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:37.020
and mix that together
and then use green grapes

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.123
to form a fist on top
of the purple yogurt.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.370
Kind of. (chuckles)

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:46.370
So next we are going to make
our Captain America burrito.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.690
And since there aren't many
burrito friendly foods that come

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.870
in the color blue, and we
want red, white, and blue.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.140
We're gonna add a little
bit of blue food coloring

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.910
to our mozzarella cheese.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.490
I'm going to add a little
salsa to my red beans,

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.970
just to give it a little more red color,

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:01.320
and to give a little more flavor.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.270
Cause Dylan does love salsa.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.610
The first layer we're
gonna add is the rice

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.160
and the rice is already white,

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.270
so we don't have to add any color to that

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:10.620
for the red, white, and blue theme.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.330
After the rice, we'll
add in our red beans.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.530
And then we'll top the whole thing off

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.330
with the blue cheese and roll it up.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.760
So now that our burritos rolled,

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.400
we're just gonna sear it off in the pan

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:24.890
to get the cheese nice and melty

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.590
and the burrito all sealed up.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.030
And now we're just gonna
cut into the burrito

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.090
and hopefully have red, white,
and blue for Captain America.

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:34.840
Next we're gonna make little
spiderwebs out of string cheese

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.500
to put underneath the strawberries,

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.190
and then we're gonna assemble everything

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.660
and put it into the box.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.440
Top those are a couple of
our Spider-man strawberries.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:45.100
Next we will pipe in some hummus

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.550
into our lightning bolt mold.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:51.950
And then we'll put the
Thor hammers around that.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.580
Now we have our already
assembled Hulk hands.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.393
We're just gonna drop this in here.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:59.790
We're going to add a
little bit of guacamole

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:00.800
for the burrito.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.463
Next we'll add our burrito.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.470
Can't forget our Captain America dessert.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:11.390
And last, just to keep
with the superheroes,

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.660
we'll add our little guys.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.747
So he knows who he's looking at.

00:11:15.747 --> 00:11:17.902
And this is the superhero lunch.

00:11:17.902 --> 00:11:21.485
(triumphant, upbeat music)

00:11:27.636 --> 00:11:31.084
- Hmm, strawberry. I don't
know how to get them out.

00:11:31.084 --> 00:11:31.968
I got it.

00:11:31.968 --> 00:11:33.635
Juicy, now I want...

00:11:34.575 --> 00:11:35.408
Avocado

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.133
- [Kelly] (laughs) Dylan.

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:42.392
- [Woman] What is it, you don't like it?

00:11:42.392 --> 00:11:43.928
- I like it.

00:11:43.928 --> 00:11:47.072
- [Producer] Did that rice
crispy remind you of anything?

00:11:47.072 --> 00:11:47.905
- No.

00:11:47.905 --> 00:11:50.277
- (laughs)

00:11:50.277 --> 00:11:52.444
- Can I have the next one?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.377
Hm. The moon.

00:11:55.377 --> 00:11:56.943
Can I take his eyes off?

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.660
This is a cold rocket ship.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:01.493
- It's what?

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.463
What was your favorite
thing out of both of these?

00:12:04.463 --> 00:12:08.440
- The strawberries and the alien.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:09.273
- Oh, the alien?

00:12:09.273 --> 00:12:10.350
You liked that cheese.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.950
Did you like your pizza?

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.423
- I didn't know that was pizza.

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.180
- Because it was cold?

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:18.331
Some people like cold pizza, Dyl.

00:12:18.331 --> 00:12:19.164
- I don't.

00:12:19.164 --> 00:12:20.259
(Kelly and Jeremy laugh)

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:22.350
- All right, we have a
tough question to ask you.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:23.183
- What?

00:12:23.183 --> 00:12:24.016
- Which one was your favorite?

00:12:24.016 --> 00:12:25.360
- Ahhh...

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:26.468
Mommy's.

00:12:26.468 --> 00:12:27.301
- Yay.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:30.530
Look at you

00:12:32.304 --> 00:12:33.190
Yay.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.553
What made it the best?

00:12:37.172 --> 00:12:38.091
The lollipop?

00:12:38.091 --> 00:12:39.654
- Yeah.

00:12:39.654 --> 00:12:41.070
- Looks like mommy's
sleeping in this weekend.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.370
- (laughs) Oh, right? I forgot.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:45.420
- And that means you get to
help me with the laundry.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.253
- No.

00:12:49.401 --> 00:12:50.643
- (in unison) Thanks for having me.

